 ### Assert on accessibility properties
 
+`XCUIElement` has no `accessibilityTraits`. Its attributes are `label`, `value`, `identifier`, `elementType`, `isEnabled`, `isSelected`, `hasFocus`, and friends; traits surface through `elementType` (the button trait makes an element a `.button`) and state traits through `isSelected` / `isEnabled`.
+
 ```swift
-let cell = app.cells["order-cell"]
-XCTAssertEqual(cell.label, "Order #1234, $42.00")
-XCTAssertTrue(cell.accessibilityTraits.contains(.button))
+let order = app.buttons["order-row"] // only matches if the element is exposed as a button
+XCTAssertTrue(order.exists)
+XCTAssertEqual(order.label, "Order #1234, $42.00")
+XCTAssertEqual(order.elementType, .button)
 ```
 
+On iOS 17+, `try app.performAccessibilityAudit()` runs the Accessibility Inspector audit checks from a UI test and fails it for each issue found.
